import PEqualNP.MetaComplexity.Helpers.RunQARemove

/-!
# Theorem QA, step C2: the squeeze, and the reduction of the row to the fifth gate

C2: if the double restriction has no circuit with five gates fewer than `C`, the circuit
`qaL` of step C1 (four gates fewer) is a minimal circuit. So the row statement (pasted
verbatim as the conclusion of `qa_core_of_gap`) follows from `qaGapC3`: under every hypothesis
of the row, `qaL` is not a minimal circuit. `qaGapC3` is the paper's Step 1 and cases A, B1,
B2 (the FP chain of `qaL` lifted back into `C`); it is NOT proved here.
-/

namespace PEqualNP.MetaComplexity.Helpers.RunFour2

